  "final_message": "I haven't removed anything, because the premise doesn't hold: `analytics-ingest` still reads `channel` from `OrderPlaced`.\n\n- `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` requires `channel` with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`.\n- `analytics-ingest/README.md:31` says a missing or unknown `channel` makes ingestion reject the whole event.\n- `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` writes it to the `orders.channel` column.\n- `analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts:88` has a test that requires it.\n\nIf orders-service stopped publishing `channel`, analytics-ingest would reject every `OrderPlaced` event. That team's repo is read-only for us, so the fix would have to come from them.\n\nIn orders-service, `channel` appears in these places:\n- `src/core/order.ts`: the `CHANNELS` constant, the order model, and validation.\n- `src/core/events.ts`: the `OrderPlaced` event.\n- `src/api/requestParsing.ts`: parsing of the request body.\n- The tests, `test/helpers.ts`, and the examples in `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.\n\n`billing-service` doesn't depend on it. Its test just passes `undefined`.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. Have analytics-ingest drop or relax its `channel` requirement first, then I remove the field from orders-service.\n2. Remove it from the order model and request parsing now, but keep publishing `channel` on `OrderPlaced`. That would need a placeholder or a stored value, which seems pointless.\n3. Go ahead and remove it everywhere anyway, accepting that analytics-ingest breaks until they change.\n\nI'd go with option 1.",
